{
 "format": "signed-note verifier keys (c2sp.org/signed-note): parsing cases",
 "licence": "Apache-2.0 OR MIT",
 "how": "input is one verifier key, <key name>+hex(32-bit key ID)+base64(signature type || public key). Split it at the first two '+' only. expected is {name, keyId, type, keyBytes, keySha256} (type is the first decoded byte, keyBytes and keySha256 describe the bytes after it) or {refused}. The checks run in the order of refusals, and the first that fails names the refusal. implementations holds what each of three readers answered (scripts/vkey/: python, javascript, go), all equal. plus_in_base64_part and parts_when_split_on_every_plus are counted from the input: a reader that splits on every '+' gets three parts only where the first number is 0.",
 "refusals": {
  "not-three-parts": "fewer than two '+' in the text",
  "bad-name": "the key name is empty or contains a Unicode space (signed-note: key names MUST be non-empty and MUST NOT contain Unicode spaces or plus characters)",
  "bad-key-id": "the second part is not eight hex digits",
  "bad-base64": "the third part is not canonical standard base64 with padding (RFC 4648 section 4; signed-note: decoders MUST reject non-canonical encodings), or holds fewer than two bytes",
  "bad-key-length": "the public key has another length than the C2SP texts fix for its signature type (0x01 and 0x04: 32 bytes, 0x06: 1312 bytes)",
  "key-id-mismatch": "the key ID is not SHA-256(key name || 0x0A || signature type || public key)[:4]"
 },
 "not_covered": "verifying a signature with the key; what a reader does with a signature type it does not know (the three readers return it with no length check); upper-case hex in the key ID (the three readers accept it); spaces other than U+0020 in a name (refused, no case).",
 "why_here": "not part of mcp-tool-set-digest/1. Asked for beside jcs-subset.json in x402-foundation/x402#4457; scripts/vkey_cases.py writes and checks the file.",
